        "text": "YUM package management system\nYUM is the default package manager for CentOS. It makes it easy to manage software packages\nby resolving dependencies and downloading required packages. With YUM, users can install new\npackages, update existing packages, and remove packages as needed. YUM provides a command line\ninterface that allows users to manage packages from the terminal, as well as a graphical user interface\nfor users who prefer a visual approach.\nPackage installation commands\n29",
